mplete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044176/state.json" "file_sha256" "dacf790fc73962be0974aac75d2ebfeea5a6e5cda1a282080b820870525fa37c"} {"question" "q-120268" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$\\lambda =3$ and $\\mu =-2$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044176/state.json" "file_sha256" "dacf790fc73962be0974aac75d2ebfeea5a6e5cda1a282080b820870525fa37c"} {"question" "q-120303" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044176/assets/50b87e86bd2985e54ce0a8fe6b3e23986f7e1946a5284d0ae297d96b9cbc60f6.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OM}=m,$ $\\overset{\\to }{ON}=n$ and $P$ divides $\\overset{―}{MN}$ in the ratio $MP:PN=2:1.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{OP}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044176/state.json" "file_sha256" "dacf790fc73962be0974aac75d2ebfeea5a6e5cda1a282080b820870525fa37c"} {"question" "q-120303" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OP}=\\overset{\\to }{OM}+\\overset{\\to }{MP}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OM}=m,$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{MP}.$\n\nFirst, from $△OMN,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{MN} & =\\overset{\\to }{MO}+\\overset{\\to }{ON} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OM}+\\overset{\\to }{ON} \\\\  & =-m+n \\\\  & =n-m.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $MP:PN=2:1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{MP}=\\frac{2}{3}\\overset{\\to }{MN}=\\frac{2}{3}(n-m).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OP} & =\\overset{\\to }{OM}+\\overset{\\to }{MP} \\\\  & =m+\\frac{2}{3}(n-m) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}m+\\frac{2}{3}n.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044176/state.json" "file_sha256" "dacf790fc73962be0974aac75d2ebfeea5a6e5cda1a282080b820870525fa37c"} {"question" "q-120303" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044176/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4f3ea802dd0f66ca870281a32fee5a331d99d3806c48f8a1e76495e29627d6a4"} {"question" "q-120303" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044176/state.json" "file_sha256" "dacf790fc73962be0974aac75d2ebfeea5a6e5cda1a282080b820870525fa37c"} {"question" "q-120303" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\overset{\\to }{OP}=\\frac{1}{2}m+\\frac{1}{2}n"] ["math" "\\overset{\\to }{OP}=\\frac{1}{3}m+\\frac{2}{3}n"] ["math" "\\overset{\\to }{OP}=\\frac{2}{3}m+\\frac{1}{3}n"] ["math" "\\overset{\\to }{OP}=\\frac{4}{9}m+\\frac{5}{9}n"] ["math" "\\overset{\\to }{OP}=\\frac{5}{9}m+\\frac{4}{9}n"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044176/state.json" "file_sha256" "dacf790fc73962be0974aac75d2ebfeea5a6e5cda1a282080b820870525fa37c"} {"question" "q-120303" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\overset{\\to }{OP}=\\frac{1}{3}m+\\frac{2}{3}n"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044176/state.json" "file_sha256" "dacf790fc73962be0974aac75d2ebfeea5a6e5cda1a282080b820870525fa37c"} {"question" "q-322583" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044176/assets/d0e71a97dc559536c25b63fda50805875d4651166a9442ae0d3d081704edebb2.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OA}=a,$ $\\overset{\\to }{OQ}=q,$ and $N$ divides $\\overset{―}{AQ}$ in the ratio $AN:NQ=12:7.$ Express $\\overset{\\to }{ON}$ via the vectors $a$ and $q.$\n\n$\\,\\overset{\\to }{ON}=$\n{{field-1}}\n$a+$\n{{field-2}}\n$q$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044176/state.json" "file_sha256" "dacf790fc73962be0974aac75d2ebfeea5a6e5cda1a282080b820870525fa37c"} {"question" "q-322583" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{ON}=\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{AN}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OA}=a,$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{AN}.$\n\nFirst, from $△OAQ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AQ} & =\\overset{\\to }{AO}+\\overset{\\to }{OQ} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{OQ} \\\\  & =-a+q \\\\  & =q-a.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $AN:NQ=12:7,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{AN}=\\frac{12}{19}\\overset{\\to }{AQ}=\\frac{12}{19}(q-a).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{ON} & =\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{AN} \\\\  & =a+\\frac{12}{19}(q-a) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{19}a+\\frac{12}{19}q.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044176/state.json" "file_sha256" "dacf790fc73962be0974aac75d2ebfeea5a6e5cda1a282080b820870525fa37c"} {"question" "q-322583" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044176/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4f3ea802dd0f66ca870281a32fee5a331d99d3806c48f8a1e76495e29627d6a4"} {"question" "q-322583" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044176/state.json" "file_sha256" "dacf790fc73962be0974aac75d2ebfeea5a6e5cda1a282080b820870525fa37c"} {"question" "q-322583" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{7}{19}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044176/state.json" "file_sha256" "dacf790fc73962be0974aac75d2ebfeea5a6e5cda1a282080b820870525fa37c"} {"question" "q-322583" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044176/state.json" "file_sha256" "dacf790fc73962be0974aac75d2ebfeea5a6e5cda1a282080b820870525fa37c"} {"question" "q-322583" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{12}{19}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044176/state.json" "file_sha256" "dacf790fc73962be0974aac75d2ebfeea5a6e5cda1a282080b820870525fa37c"} {"question" "q-367064" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044176/assets/80cedeceb8d377617af880cab1c383643e3cd79055eccce046b0418598897ac8.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. If $c=\\lambda a-2b,$ then$\\,\\lambda =$\n{{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044176/state.json" "file_sha256" "dacf790fc73962be0974aac75d2ebfeea5a6e5cda1a282080b820870525fa37c"} {"question" "q-367064" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find $\\lambda ,$ we want to match the expression\n\n$$\nc=\\lambda a-2b.\n$$\n\nWe are given that one of the components is $-2b.$ So, we first draw the vector $-2b$ from the origin. Then we complete the path to the point $C.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044176/assets/7e6923e8b8b774eeaa2f885ec6aa24bb03f07c547fa50e7145a4113a18e92e8a.png)\n\nLet $P$ be the endpoint of the vector $-2b.$ Then\n\n$$\nc=\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PC}.\n$$\n\nIn $△OPC,$ we have:\n\n- $PC=2|a|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{PC}$ and $a$ have opposite directions\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{PC}=-2a.$\n\nAdditionally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PC} \\\\  & =-2b-2a.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $c=\\lambda a-2b=-2a-2b.$\n\nSince $a∦b,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients of $a,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\lambda =-2\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044176/state.json" "file_sha256" "dacf790fc73962be0974aac75d2ebfeea5a6e5cda1a282080b820870525fa37c"} {"question" "q-367064" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044176/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4f3ea802dd0f66ca870281a32fee5a331d99d3806c48f8a1e76495e29627d6a4"} {"question" "q-367064" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044176/state.json" "file_sha256" "dacf790fc73962be0974aac75d2ebfeea5a6e5cda1a282080b820870525fa37c"} {"question" "q-367064" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044176/state.json" "file_sha256" "dacf790fc73962be0974aac75d2ebfeea5a6e5cda1a282080b820870525fa37c"}] "usage" {"q-42670" []} "basis" 1640 "retractions" [[17592186097160 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1106/Source/Images/q-42670.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. Given that $t = λr + μs$, find $λ$ and $μ$."] [17592186097160 :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13938412/assets/a0d9fa1c366945e5e789b6361f929357af163db2e9be4a3ccc9023c12486aca6.png)\n\nIn $△ORT$ shown above, we have:\n\n- $OR=2|r|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{OR}$ has the opposite direction to $r$\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{OR}=-2r.$\n\nSimilarly:\n\n- $RT=2|s|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{RT}$ has the opposite direction to $s$\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{RT}=-2s.$\n\nAdditionally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t & =\\overset{\\to }{OR}+\\overset{\\to }{RT} \\\\  & =-2r-2s.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $t=\\lambda r+\\mu s=-2r-2s.$ \n\nSince $s∦r,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients, we get:\n\n- $\\lambda =-2$ and $\\mu =-2$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186095318 17592186095319 17592186095320 17592186095321 17592186095322] "immutable_fields" [[17592186095317 :answer-field/correct] [17592186095317 :answer-field/id] [17592186095317 :answer-field/key] [17592186095317 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
